<%# A miniature window drawn in the theme's own tokens: navbar strip, sidebar
    column, content area, accent dot. The element carries the theme class, so
    the class-scoped variables in the theme's stylesheet resolve here as they
    do on <html>. Derived tokens are re-declared on .theme-tile (see
    color_scheme_switcher.css) so a theme that only sets primitives still
    previews correctly. %>
<span class="theme-tile <%= theme.css_class %>" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="theme-tile__navbar"></span>
  <span class="theme-tile__sidebar"></span>
  <span class="theme-tile__content"></span>
  <span class="theme-tile__accent"></span>
</span>
